id: notes/source-bound-overlap-review
kind: architecture-review
status: completed-working-review
updated: 2026-09-01
reviewer: agent:openai:gpt-5.6-pro
reviewed:
  - pull_request: 23
    title: "Coordinate-complete cognition: type move selection, rightful choice, and New Yawn projection"
  - pull_request: 24
    title: "Proposal: coordinate-complete New Yawn workbench"
  - pull_request: 25
    title: "Compile New Yawn into coordinate-complete resolution"
  - pull_request: 26
    title: "Define source-bound Yawnbots and criterion-relative Evaluation"

finding: >
  PRs 23, 24, and 25 are nearby attempts to close the same New Yawn and move-selection seam. They should not be merged independently as three parallel canonical stories. PR 26 correctly remains stacked on the smaller PR 25 projection and adds a downstream source-bound grammar rather than another Orientation Map, resolution ladder, inquiry selector, or move selector.

pr_23:
  unique_value:
    - explicit rightful Choice Event schema
    - strongest full path from recommendation through choice, authority, execution, consequence, proof, and update
    - adversarial tests for recommendation-choice-authorization separation
  overlap:
    - move-selection receipt
    - coordinate-complete New Yawn View
    - core and interface index edits
  disposition: >
    Preserve the Choice Event work as a candidate focused follow-on. Do not copy its entire alternative New Yawn interface or second move-selection story into PR 26. PR 26 therefore uses an external choiceEventRef and keeps the absence of an accepted Choice Event contract visible.

pr_24:
  unique_value:
    - runtime compiler, backfill, and correction-path experiments
    - detailed coordinate header and workbench View
    - explicit intelligence-binding readout
  overlap:
    - parallel New Yawn workbench contract
    - parallel resolution grid and level semantics
    - parallel schema and compiler path
  disposition: >
    Treat PR 24 as an implementation experiment to mine after the semantic contract settles. Do not merge its parallel workbench schema beside PR 25 without a deliberate port or retirement decision. Reuse only unique runtime/backfill ideas that conform to the accepted projection.

pr_25:
  unique_value:
    - smallest coordinate-complete noncanonical View
    - proposal-only Auto-lacuna and Auto-cohere
    - compact move-selection receipt without redefining choice
  overlap:
    - parent substrate for PR 26
  disposition: >
    Keep PR 26 stacked on PR 25. PR 25 owns coordinate resolution and move-selection proposal semantics; PR 26 owns preserved source compilation, Position-as-Answer, expression provision, Character View, Consequence, criterion-relative Evaluation, Proof separation, Update, and recursion.

pr_26_boundary:
  owns:
    - source-bound mental-model aggregate
    - recursive passage as a View
    - Evaluation as canonical term with Judgment as interface alias
    - source-to-proposal correction and ratification boundary
    - expression-provision versus Projection distinction
    - Nestheads/Kickstarter sanitized dogfood fixture
  does_not_own:
    - another Orientation Map
    - another coordinate resolution ladder
    - another inquiry selector
    - a second move selector
    - canonical Choice Event
    - runtime compiler or database migration
    - production UI or publication

recommended_sequence:
  - validate PR 26 on the exact stacked head
  - owner-review PR 25 and PR 26 together as distinct layers
  - decide whether to extract PR 23 Choice Event into a focused additive draft
  - either port PR 24 runtime/backfill ideas onto the chosen contract or close it as superseded experiment
  - only then implement the product workbench and persistence layer

risk_if_ignored:
  - duplicate source-of-truth contracts
  - conflicting resolution metrics
  - recommendation and choice semantics drifting by interface
  - two parallel workbench schemas
  - future agents selecting whichever draft best fits their preferred answer

boundary:
  - "This review does not close, merge, supersede, or authorize any pull request."
  - "Choice Event remains a candidate contract, not silently accepted canon."
  - "Runtime implementation remains downstream of semantic owner review."
  - "Exact-head CI remains separate proof."